<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Feltrino Gonzaga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1374</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Feltrino Gonzaga was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aloysius-gonzaga">Luigi Gonzaga</a>, the first Gonzaga lord of Mantua. He ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reggio-emilia">Reggio Emilia</a> as its lord from the 1330s until 1371, when he gave up the city to the Visconti of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, keeping only Novellara and Bagnolo in the plain to the north. These lands became the County of Novellara, held by his descendants, a cadet branch of the Gonzaga, until the line died out in 1728.</p></div>
